1
00:00:03,054 --> 00:00:05,283
Tonight, the Moon is a thin crescent,

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:07,684
but last week, it was completely round!

3
00:00:07,734 --> 00:00:09,582
Did someone eat a piece of it?

4
00:00:10,388 --> 00:00:12,364
Mila drew it all: every night,

5
00:00:12,414 --> 00:00:14,121
the Moon changes a little.

6
00:00:14,171 --> 00:00:16,535
And yet, it's always the same Moon!

7
00:00:17,312 --> 00:00:18,826
Discovery mission!

8
00:00:21,342 --> 00:00:21,967
Mini mode!

9
00:00:22,017 --> 00:00:25,074
The Sun always lights up one half of the Moon,

10
00:00:25,124 --> 00:00:25,546
always!

11
00:00:25,596 --> 00:00:28,095
And the other half stays in the dark.

12
00:00:28,871 --> 00:00:30,295
But the Moon goes around

13
00:00:30,345 --> 00:00:31,585
the Earth in a month.

14
00:00:31,635 --> 00:00:32,753
So, from your home,

15
00:00:32,803 --> 00:00:36,488
you see its lit half from an angle that changes every night.

16
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:39,944
A small piece is a crescent.

17
00:00:39,994 --> 00:00:41,764
Half of it is a quarter.

18
00:00:41,814 --> 00:00:43,508
And the whole lit half…

19
00:00:43,558 --> 00:00:44,797
is the full Moon!

20
00:00:44,847 --> 00:00:47,350
Then it shrinks and starts again.

21
00:00:48,121 --> 00:00:51,216
And from space, Curio sees the Moon half and half,

22
00:00:51,266 --> 00:00:54,235
one side facing the Sun, the other in the night.

23
00:00:54,285 --> 00:00:55,858
So it never lost a piece!

24
00:00:56,641 --> 00:00:58,943
And that's why the Moon changes shape.

25
00:01:00,199 --> 00:01:02,497
The Moon is always half lit by the Sun;

26
00:01:02,547 --> 00:01:04,715
it's our viewing angle that changes.

27
00:01:05,641 --> 00:01:08,462
With an adult, in the dark: turn on a lamp,

28
00:01:08,512 --> 00:01:11,935
hold a ball at arm's length, and turn around slowly…

29
00:01:11,985 --> 00:01:13,921
crescent, quarter, full Moon!

30
00:01:14,691 --> 00:01:17,361
And why do we hear thunder after lightning?

31
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:18,676
The answer tomorrow.
